WEBVTT

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:10.820
Request from Ichigo... when watching the television, sit a safe distance from the television in a well-lit room.

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:08.860
we started thinking about the finals and headed to the market to scout ingredients!

00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:13.970
Would you like to try one, Miss?

00:00:13.970 --> 00:00:14.990
Merci!

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:22.350
French strawberries are sweet and delicious!

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:23.860
My tongue is gonna melt!

00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:26.160
Sheesh, how much snacking do you plan on doing?

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:28.500
I'm tasting! Tasting...

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:31.510
If you taste it, then take responsibility and buy some!

00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:32.650
Kashino...

00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:34.350
I know, geez!

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:36.550
I just have to buy some, right!?

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:37.970
Donnez-moi ceci.

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:40.750
Where did you go?

00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:43.040
I went to the Paris campus library to get this.

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:44.440
What is that?

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:47.650
This is a recipe book of famous pâtissiers.

00:00:47.650 --> 00:00:50.510
Using this as a reference, you can study a ton!

00:00:50.510 --> 00:00:51.960
Recipes, huh?

00:00:52.250 --> 00:00:58.100
If the recipe hadn't vanished, I could make my grandma's strawberry tart with these strawberries...

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:00.660
OP sequence

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:00.890
Are you talking about your grandmother's recipe that you mentioned before?

00:01:00.890 --> 00:01:01.490
Yeah.

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:07.200
I finally managed to open the lock, but for some reason, the page with the strawberry tart recipe was blank!

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:12.540
That's odd. I'm sure it was an important recipe, so she should have written it down like this.

00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:14.690
Ah, Kashino!

00:01:14.690 --> 00:01:16.400
Look at this!

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:18.510
W-What's this?

00:01:23.830 --> 00:01:30.100
fuwa fuwa funwari amakute toro kechau

00:01:23.830 --> 00:01:30.100
Fluffy, fluffy, fluffiness, so sweetly it melts.

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:35.470
shiawase wo ageru yo yumeiro no pâtishièeru<i>!!</i>

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:35.470
I'll give you happiness, the dream-coloured Pâtissière<i>!!</i>

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:40.970
ichigo furejie & furanbowaazu, hapihapi makaron, hapinesu made go!

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:40.970
Strawberry Fraisier & Framboise, happy happy Macaron, Happiness made go!

00:01:40.970 --> 00:01:46.140
chansu no tobira aketa toki kara kibun joujou ↑ ↑

00:01:40.970 --> 00:01:46.140
Since I opened the door of chance, my mood lifted.

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:50.100
youkoso suiitsu no oukoku he

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:50.100
Welcome to the Kingdom of Sweets.

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:51.020
Bon appétit!

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:58.400
hajimehane, hetappi demo megezu ni hibishoujin<i>!</i>

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:58.400
Though I was terrible at the beginning, I was diligent everyday<i>!</i>

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:01.030
「makeruna<i>! atashi」</i>

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:01.030
「I won't lose<i>!</i> I said to myself」

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:02.040
Courage!

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:08.820
My dream migakeba hikaru takaramono

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:08.820
My dream when polished is a shining treasure.

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:11.540
fairy chikara kashite<i>!</i>

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:11.540
Fairy, lend me your strength<i>!</i>

00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:16.960
shifon, se shibon, juré, bonjuuru, hatsuratsu furuutsu, raburii made go!

00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:16.960
Chiffon, C'est si bon, Gelée, Bonjour, Lively fruits, Lovely made go!

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:23.050
nakitaku natte mo egao ni nareru mahou

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:23.050
Even if you cry, there is magic that can make you smile.

00:02:23.050 --> 00:02:28.270
「oishii<i>!」 wo tsukurutte omoikkiri tanoshii ne</i>

00:02:23.050 --> 00:02:28.270
「Delicious<i>!</i>」 and making it wholeheartedly is fun.

00:02:28.270 --> 00:02:34.270
fuwa fuwa funwari amakute toro kechau

00:02:28.270 --> 00:02:34.270
Fluffy, fluffy, fluffiness, so sweetly it melts.

00:02:34.270 --> 00:02:39.610
shiawase wo ageru yo yumeiro no pâtishièeru<i>!!</i>

00:02:34.270 --> 00:02:39.610
I'll give happiness to you, the dream-coloured Pâtissière<i>!!</i>

00:02:39.610 --> 00:02:44.160
ichigo furejie & furanbowaazu, hapihapi makaron, fun fun

00:02:39.610 --> 00:02:44.160
Strawberry Fraisier & Framboise, happy happy Macaron, fun, fun

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:46.370
yume ni eeru<i>!</i>

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:46.370
Get them in our dreams<i>!</i>

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:50.920
Presented by Wasurenai-subs

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:58.520
Good morning. Yumeiro Pâtissière is brought to you by Konami and these other sponsors.

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:04.690
I knew it! It's just like my grandma's recipe book!

00:03:04.690 --> 00:03:10.200
I can't believe that books from France and Japan both have recipes that disappeared...

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:14.720
Even though this book is printed with very old ink...

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:15.440
That's it!

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:16.550
Maybe...

00:03:17.350 --> 00:03:18.810
What are you going to do?

00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:19.960
Invisible ink!

00:03:19.960 --> 00:03:21.560
Just like in police dramas...

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:24.220
Crucial information might have been written with sugar water!

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:26.140
Don't!

00:03:27.170 --> 00:03:28.300
H-H-Hey!

00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:35.550
Sheesh... Treat it more carefully, would you?

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:37.510
That's...

00:03:40.170 --> 00:03:42.850
It's the same as us Sweets Spirits!

00:03:42.850 --> 00:03:45.870
And it's not from the four of us!

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:47.260
What does that mean?

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:52.100
It means that the recipes vanishing might have something to do with Sweets Spirits.

00:03:52.390 --> 00:03:56.800
Maybe there is some reason to bring the recipes to the Kingdom of Sweets?

00:03:56.800 --> 00:04:01.170
It seems plausible, but I've never heard of such a thing before.

00:04:01.610 --> 00:04:03.880
Then let's go ask!

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:08.550
I got the key to grandma's recipe book in the Kingdom of Sweets, too...

00:04:08.550 --> 00:04:11.670
I think that person might have been my grandma's Spirit!

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:15.140
She might know what happened to the missing recipe.

00:04:15.470 --> 00:04:18.350
I'll go check out the Kingdom of Sweets!

00:04:18.350 --> 00:04:20.320
Are you sure?

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:22.880
It's a crucial time before the finals...

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:23.980
Is there time for this?

00:04:23.980 --> 00:04:27.040
No, it's <i>because</i> it's before the finals I have to go!

00:04:28.170 --> 00:04:31.410
The theme and subject haven't been announced yet,

00:04:31.410 --> 00:04:35.990
but if I have the chance, I want to make my grandma's strawberry tart for the finals!

00:04:35.990 --> 00:04:43.760
With such wonderful strawberries, if I only had the recipe, my grandma's beloved strawberry tart could live again, for sure!

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:44.970
I see.

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:47.260
If you feel so strongly about it, Amano-san.

00:04:47.260 --> 00:04:48.880
Are you sure you are fine with that?

00:04:49.420 --> 00:04:54.490
I checked out that recipe book solely to study techniques.

00:04:54.950 --> 00:04:56.760
It wasn't so I could copy them exactly.

00:04:58.580 --> 00:05:04.640
We pâtissiers should do battle with our own original flavours and creations, not the work of others.

00:05:05.050 --> 00:05:06.650
That's what I think.

00:05:07.460 --> 00:05:08.800
Well...

00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:11.180
Anyway, if you're going, go by yourself.

00:05:11.180 --> 00:05:13.530
I have plenty to do here.

00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:18.150
Fine!

00:05:18.150 --> 00:05:21.480
I was planning on going by myself anyway!

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:24.120
I don't need you to save me, Kashino, hmph!

00:05:25.290 --> 00:05:26.580
Please.

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:28.700
I don't mind, but...

00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:30.450
Caramel, go with them.

00:05:30.450 --> 00:05:31.790
Roger!

00:05:31.790 --> 00:05:34.170
I'd be worried if Vanilla went alone!

00:05:34.170 --> 00:05:35.460
You too, Cafe-kun.

00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:36.030
Yes.

00:05:36.030 --> 00:05:36.800
I will accompany you.

00:05:37.050 --> 00:05:40.130
I'm also curious about that missing recipe.

00:05:40.130 --> 00:05:42.530
Kashino, you don't mind, right?

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:44.230
Suit yourself.

00:05:44.420 --> 00:05:50.390
recipe 46

00:05:44.420 --> 00:05:50.390
Grandma's Recipe

00:05:54.910 --> 00:05:57.570
Sorry about this, Andou-kun, Hanabusa-kun...

00:05:57.570 --> 00:05:59.850
I'll do my best to be back before nighttime.

00:05:59.850 --> 00:06:00.450
Right.

00:06:00.450 --> 00:06:02.580
Come on, see her off too, Kashino.

00:06:06.710 --> 00:06:07.970
Why you little...

00:06:08.910 --> 00:06:12.020
Where did you meet the old lady?

00:06:12.020 --> 00:06:14.480
I think it was inside the mysterious forest...

00:06:15.900 --> 00:06:18.060
Where was it again?

00:06:18.060 --> 00:06:20.940
Umm, do you think you've gotten lost already?

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:24.870
N-No, not at all...

00:06:25.170 --> 00:06:26.880
I'll find it, really!

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:30.190
If I recall, I was running through the forest,

00:06:30.190 --> 00:06:32.650
then I suddenly fell into a hole,

00:06:32.650 --> 00:06:35.480
and right after I fell, the old lady...

00:06:38.490 --> 00:06:39.330
There it is!

00:06:39.330 --> 00:06:40.410
It's that forest!

00:06:40.410 --> 00:06:41.490
Wait!

00:06:44.150 --> 00:06:45.230
Ichigo!

00:06:45.230 --> 00:06:46.290
Are you okay?

00:06:46.540 --> 00:06:48.540
What the heck is this?

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:50.880
I have a feeling this has happened before...

00:06:51.350 --> 00:06:52.450
Oh, come on now...

00:06:52.450 --> 00:06:55.000
I thought we'd caught dinner, but it's just you guys!

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:56.100
That voice!

00:06:58.650 --> 00:07:00.110
It's the Jerk Brigade!

00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:03.050
Not anymore!

00:07:03.300 --> 00:07:08.350
Chocolate is my specialty!
Tempering king, Kashi!

00:07:08.350 --> 00:07:12.930
If it's red beans, I'm the Kingdom of Sweets number 1.
Nenderu Andi!

00:07:12.930 --> 00:07:20.560
My Sweets Crafting can melt any girls' heart.
Rose's count, Narcy.

00:07:20.820 --> 00:07:24.000
The three of us are the Sweets Princes!

00:07:29.950 --> 00:07:31.260
I see!

00:07:31.260 --> 00:07:34.900
So you came to the Kingdom of Sweets in search of a recipe that disappeared.

00:07:34.900 --> 00:07:35.590
Yeah.

00:07:35.590 --> 00:07:38.500
My real name is Amano Ichigo.

00:07:38.500 --> 00:07:41.580
I'm actually a human. Sorry for not telling you before.

00:07:41.580 --> 00:07:43.590
Don't worry, Ichigo-chan.

00:07:43.590 --> 00:07:49.850
I love human girls and Spirit girls all the same!

00:07:49.850 --> 00:07:52.850
I really don't think that was the issue...

00:07:52.850 --> 00:07:59.150
If a recipe from the human world was brought into the Kingdom, then it can only be in one place.

00:07:59.670 --> 00:08:00.200
Where?

00:08:00.850 --> 00:08:02.960
The Court Pâtissier Museum!

00:08:07.600 --> 00:08:11.910
I stole a Court Pâtissier recipe from here once.

00:08:11.910 --> 00:08:15.350
And the Queen got very mad when you were found out.

00:08:15.350 --> 00:08:18.020
Well, I really regret it now, okay?

00:08:18.020 --> 00:08:18.760
Anyway!

00:08:19.410 --> 00:08:23.770
When I was there, I noticed another room inside that was sealed off.

00:08:23.770 --> 00:08:28.200
The rumor is that it holds truly incredible recipes from the human world.

00:08:29.260 --> 00:08:33.230
Then that means that grandma's recipe might be in there!

00:08:33.230 --> 00:08:36.450
Let's go ask the Queen for a peek right away!

00:08:37.350 --> 00:08:43.300
Impossible. Only the Queen and a very limited few of high social status are allowed inside.

00:08:43.300 --> 00:08:44.790
That's why we came through here.

00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:47.290
You're not thinking of...

00:08:48.250 --> 00:08:49.840
Indeed we are!

00:08:49.950 --> 00:08:51.450
Let's go, Ichigo-chan!

00:08:52.400 --> 00:08:53.450
Hey!

00:08:54.740 --> 00:08:56.610
You guys wait here.

00:08:56.610 --> 00:08:58.460
After we find the recipe, we'll be right back!

00:08:58.710 --> 00:09:00.650
I'm her partner!

00:09:00.650 --> 00:09:02.400
If Ichigo goes, I go!

00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:03.170
Wait, Vanilla!

00:09:03.440 --> 00:09:05.300
If you're discovered you'll get in big trouble!

00:09:05.300 --> 00:09:06.130
Who's there?

00:09:06.470 --> 00:09:08.050
What are you doing here?

00:09:10.700 --> 00:09:14.390
I'm sorry!

00:09:14.770 --> 00:09:18.110
Please pretend like you didn't see us!

00:09:18.110 --> 00:09:19.980
Please, I beg of you!

00:09:19.980 --> 00:09:21.760
C-Caramel...

00:09:21.760 --> 00:09:22.790
You're strong...

00:09:22.790 --> 00:09:25.990
Well, she is the oldest out of us...

00:09:26.410 --> 00:09:29.360
I guess she's pretty useful for times like this...

00:09:44.130 --> 00:09:45.710
Oh, it's a candy sculpture....

00:09:45.710 --> 00:09:48.000
Be quiet! They'll discover us!

00:09:48.760 --> 00:09:50.450
Wow...

00:09:50.450 --> 00:09:55.300
Look at all the different sweets on display here in the Kingdom of Sweets' Museum!

00:09:55.300 --> 00:10:01.260
Chocolate and candy sculptures can last for tens or even hundreds of years with proper maintenance.

00:10:01.260 --> 00:10:03.340
They really are beautiful...

00:10:04.650 --> 00:10:07.200
This is no time to be awestruck.

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:08.530
What'll happen if we're found out?

00:10:09.570 --> 00:10:11.130
We're here! It's inside here.

00:10:15.240 --> 00:10:18.290
Damn it, it's locked after all...

00:10:23.070 --> 00:10:25.430
Ichigo, your spoon is glowing!

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:29.630
It has the same symbol!

00:10:29.910 --> 00:10:31.470
Then, I'll use this to...

00:10:36.790 --> 00:10:38.480
It actually opened!

00:10:41.180 --> 00:10:43.490
Grandma's recipe is in here...

00:10:48.350 --> 00:10:49.450
Shoot!

00:10:59.350 --> 00:11:02.650
Save me!

00:11:07.050 --> 00:11:09.550
I told you they'd be found!

00:11:09.550 --> 00:11:14.410
Then we have no choice but to take these guards' clothes and sneak inside!

00:11:14.410 --> 00:11:15.340
Whoa there...

00:11:15.340 --> 00:11:18.240
Calm down Caramel, that'll really get us in trouble!

00:11:18.560 --> 00:11:23.060
Director, the intruders have been locked in the basement cell for the time being.

00:11:23.500 --> 00:11:26.010
I wonder how they managed to get into that room?

00:11:26.440 --> 00:11:28.550
It should be impossible, no matter what magic you use!

00:11:28.550 --> 00:11:29.650
Well, about that...

00:11:29.650 --> 00:11:32.620
They were carrying these.

00:11:33.210 --> 00:11:34.450
That's...

00:11:34.930 --> 00:11:36.840
Summon the former Director at once!

00:11:37.030 --> 00:11:40.800
I wonder if I'll ever get to return home...

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:46.500
I'm sure the Queen will forgive you when she hears what happened since you're a human, Ichigo-chan.

00:11:46.500 --> 00:11:50.530
But the Queen got mad at you three before, right?

00:11:50.530 --> 00:11:52.100
And now Vanilla...

00:11:53.830 --> 00:11:56.220
I bet my spoon will be taken away...

00:11:56.220 --> 00:11:58.530
We'll revert back to being the Jerk Brigade.

00:11:58.530 --> 00:12:01.450
But it'll be the four of us together! That's not so bad.

00:12:01.450 --> 00:12:03.200
Hey, wait a minute!

00:12:03.200 --> 00:12:05.860
I'm not gonna be a member of the Jerk Brigade!

00:12:06.590 --> 00:12:07.910
I'm sorry...

00:12:08.350 --> 00:12:11.290
I knew this would happen if we got caught, and yet...

00:12:11.540 --> 00:12:13.240
This is my fault.

00:12:14.170 --> 00:12:15.990
I'm sorry, really.

00:12:16.540 --> 00:12:17.970
Don't cry.

00:12:19.440 --> 00:12:22.940
You said our sweets were delicious, remember?

00:12:24.470 --> 00:12:29.560
You said that if the Queen tried some of our sweets, she might forgive us.

00:12:30.210 --> 00:12:33.810
When you told us that, it cheered us up when we were sad.

00:12:34.560 --> 00:12:43.480
It's because of your words that the Queen pardoned us, and we've been working hard after that.

00:12:43.480 --> 00:12:46.650
So we wanted to help you to return the favour.

00:12:46.650 --> 00:12:52.230
And if I get the chance to be with you again, I'll do my best no matter how difficult the punishment is!

00:12:53.170 --> 00:12:54.750
I'm sorry, everyone...

00:12:55.450 --> 00:12:57.450
We're sorry, too.

00:12:57.450 --> 00:12:59.410
We weren't able to find your recipe.

00:12:59.410 --> 00:13:00.420
No...

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:04.460
I wanted to make my grandma's strawberry tart, but it can't be helped.

00:13:04.850 --> 00:13:07.460
Why do you keep dwelling on that strawberry tart?

00:13:08.120 --> 00:13:15.970
Because it's a magical sweet that brought a smile to my face every time I was feeling down as a child.

00:13:17.840 --> 00:13:23.150
I want to recreate that taste, and bring smiles to everyone just like grandma did!

00:13:23.740 --> 00:13:25.350
I see.

00:13:25.350 --> 00:13:27.840
But that's not your taste.

00:13:28.850 --> 00:13:31.930
I stole a recipe and made it just like it said.

00:13:32.500 --> 00:13:37.390
But no matter how many people told me it was delicious, it didn't make me happy.

00:13:38.300 --> 00:13:40.380
Because it was a taste created by someone else!

00:13:41.350 --> 00:13:47.350
True happiness comes when someone says a sweet that you created yourself tastes delicious.

00:13:47.740 --> 00:13:51.700
Like when you said our cookies were delicious, Ichigo.

00:13:52.310 --> 00:13:56.640
We should do battle with our own original flavours and creations, not the work of others.

00:13:56.920 --> 00:13:58.930
That's just what Kashino said...

00:13:59.580 --> 00:14:00.500
What?

00:14:00.940 --> 00:14:01.850
Nothing.

00:14:06.790 --> 00:14:08.410
You two, come with me.

00:14:12.040 --> 00:14:14.470
It is not me whom you have business with.

00:14:14.900 --> 00:14:17.690
It is the former Director over there.

00:14:18.640 --> 00:14:22.830
It has been a while, human girl.

00:14:22.830 --> 00:14:25.010
It's the old lady from before!

00:14:25.010 --> 00:14:26.550
Yes.

00:14:26.550 --> 00:14:29.630
It seems you've opened Michiko's recipe book...

00:14:30.120 --> 00:14:31.460
I knew it!

00:14:31.460 --> 00:14:33.810
You were my grandma's spirit, right?

00:14:36.020 --> 00:14:38.550
I noticed you in the town and realised it immediately.

00:14:39.350 --> 00:14:42.830
"This girl must be Michiko's granddaughter, no doubt."

00:14:42.830 --> 00:14:47.850
I thought if I gave you the key, you would eventually come back here.

00:14:47.850 --> 00:14:52.730
But, I didn't think you'd come in such a reckless way.

00:14:52.730 --> 00:14:54.350
S-Sorry about that.

00:14:54.950 --> 00:14:57.960
But, please forgive everyone else!

00:14:57.960 --> 00:15:01.410
It's because I told them I wanted to see the strawberry tart recipe no matter what, so...

00:15:02.700 --> 00:15:05.400
You want to see it no matter what?

00:15:05.400 --> 00:15:06.730
Y-Yes...

00:15:07.120 --> 00:15:10.430
Really? You want to see it?

00:15:14.630 --> 00:15:17.640
Then please taste these.

00:15:18.250 --> 00:15:20.140
Grandma's strawberry tarts!

00:15:20.890 --> 00:15:22.580
This is a test.

00:15:23.010 --> 00:15:27.100
One of these is made according to the recipe.

00:15:27.100 --> 00:15:32.290
If you can tell me which one, I will show you the recipe.

00:15:32.700 --> 00:15:37.710
And I will also release your captured friends.

00:15:39.150 --> 00:15:40.070
Understood.

00:15:40.070 --> 00:15:41.240
I'll do it!

00:15:41.500 --> 00:15:42.610
Ichigo...

00:15:42.610 --> 00:15:43.360
Don't worry.

00:15:43.730 --> 00:15:45.400
It's a taste I love.

00:15:45.400 --> 00:15:46.330
I'll be able to tell.

00:15:52.050 --> 00:15:54.680
This isn't sweet enough.

00:15:54.680 --> 00:15:57.470
And the strawberries don't have the right crispness either...

00:15:58.240 --> 00:15:59.610
It's not this one.

00:15:59.860 --> 00:16:01.500
Continue.

00:16:06.820 --> 00:16:12.120
This one is close, but the way the dough is baked, and the roughness on the tongue...

00:16:12.120 --> 00:16:14.430
It's just a little, but I sense something is off.

00:16:15.350 --> 00:16:16.790
It's not this one either.

00:16:17.400 --> 00:16:18.990
This is the last one.

00:16:20.020 --> 00:16:21.420
This is the last!

00:16:21.420 --> 00:16:23.530
It has got to be the one!

00:16:29.070 --> 00:16:31.410
The batter, the sweetness, this flavour...

00:16:32.380 --> 00:16:33.790
What's the matter Ichigo?

00:16:33.790 --> 00:16:34.920
It's not it...

00:16:35.310 --> 00:16:37.330
Something isn't right...

00:16:39.000 --> 00:16:40.060
What is it?

00:16:40.480 --> 00:16:43.550
What is different about grandma's strawberry tart?

00:16:44.450 --> 00:16:45.480
Ichigo...

00:16:45.680 --> 00:16:47.690
What is it, grandma?

00:16:47.890 --> 00:16:58.750
If you raise strawberries one at a time like they were your own children, they'll become really delicious.

00:16:59.680 --> 00:17:01.200
Oh, really?

00:17:01.200 --> 00:17:02.050
Here!

00:17:02.050 --> 00:17:03.720
Try one.

00:17:07.250 --> 00:17:09.750
You're right! It's delicious!

00:17:09.750 --> 00:17:11.410
Now try this one too.

00:17:16.060 --> 00:17:18.160
Huh, I wonder why...

00:17:18.160 --> 00:17:20.730
Why is that one a little bitter?

00:17:20.730 --> 00:17:23.410
Wow, it's amazing you can tell!

00:17:23.410 --> 00:17:25.500
You're so wonderful, Ichigo.

00:17:25.500 --> 00:17:28.650
But why, even though they grew together?

00:17:29.090 --> 00:17:32.710
That's because the soil is different.

00:17:32.710 --> 00:17:37.260
The ones here are planted in special soil I brought in from another place.

00:17:38.710 --> 00:17:39.410
That's it...

00:17:41.190 --> 00:17:42.880
The taste of the strawberries is different.

00:17:43.250 --> 00:17:49.440
I can't make grandma's strawberry tart unless I use the strawberries that she grew in that special soil.

00:17:49.910 --> 00:17:51.900
So, this one is also wrong!

00:17:54.120 --> 00:17:55.750
Correct.

00:17:55.750 --> 00:17:57.550
All right, Ichigo!

00:17:57.550 --> 00:18:00.320
Umm, why did you give me this test?

00:18:00.320 --> 00:18:02.850
It's something Michiko left for me to do.

00:18:02.850 --> 00:18:03.840
From grandma?

00:18:03.840 --> 00:18:08.190
"My granddaughter has the most magnificent palate I've ever seen."

00:18:08.560 --> 00:18:12.350
"One day, she may aim to become a pâtissière."

00:18:13.170 --> 00:18:19.790
"And, she may come in search of the recipe for the strawberry tart,

00:18:19.790 --> 00:18:24.980
which had been selected as a Court Recipe and had vanished from the human world."

00:18:24.980 --> 00:18:31.910
"If such a time comes, I wish for you to test whether she has truly grown as a pâtissière."

00:18:31.910 --> 00:18:34.870
She asked me to test you.

00:18:35.300 --> 00:18:37.380
Grandma predicted all this?

00:18:38.280 --> 00:18:41.260
But the rest is up to you.

00:18:55.300 --> 00:18:56.490
That's...

00:18:56.490 --> 00:18:59.050
The language of the Sweets Spirits!

00:19:00.360 --> 00:19:03.460
Whether or not you read it is up to you.

00:19:03.720 --> 00:19:08.280
As you are now, you should be able to come to your own conclusion.

00:19:08.280 --> 00:19:11.080
As I am now?

00:19:13.160 --> 00:19:14.500
Everyone!

00:19:14.500 --> 00:19:17.290
Now, hurry and go.

00:19:17.980 --> 00:19:21.260
I will keep what happened today a secret.

00:19:21.260 --> 00:19:22.220
Okay!

00:19:22.220 --> 00:19:23.730
Thank you very much!

00:19:24.060 --> 00:19:26.630
Umm, Mrs. Former Director...

00:19:26.630 --> 00:19:27.890
What is it?

00:19:27.890 --> 00:19:30.660
Will you tell me your name?

00:19:30.660 --> 00:19:32.590
It's Marjoram.

00:19:32.840 --> 00:19:38.230
Marjoram-san, please let me hear stories
about my grandma sometime, okay?

00:19:45.390 --> 00:19:46.850
Oww...

00:19:46.850 --> 00:19:48.040
Ichigo-chan!

00:19:48.040 --> 00:19:48.570
Welcome back!

00:19:49.170 --> 00:19:51.280
Sorry I'm late.

00:19:51.280 --> 00:19:53.490
We had a lot of trouble!

00:19:53.490 --> 00:19:54.340
Seriously.

00:19:54.340 --> 00:19:56.280
I'm surprised we managed to make it back today.

00:19:59.480 --> 00:20:00.290
Kashino...

00:20:00.860 --> 00:20:02.930
He complained the whole time...

00:20:02.930 --> 00:20:05.350
"It's better if she doesn't find that recipe", he said.

00:20:06.210 --> 00:20:07.200
Kashino...

00:20:09.370 --> 00:20:11.280
Oh, Amano?

00:20:12.540 --> 00:20:13.980
Did you find the recipe?

00:20:15.250 --> 00:20:15.970
Yeah...

00:20:16.710 --> 00:20:17.800
What'll you do?

00:20:17.800 --> 00:20:20.860
I can use my magic to turn it into Japanese, if you want...

00:20:22.730 --> 00:20:27.300
We should do battle with our own original flavours and creations, not the work of others.

00:20:27.840 --> 00:20:34.010
True happiness comes when someone says a sweet that you created yourself tastes delicious.

00:20:36.040 --> 00:20:39.390
Don't worry, you don't have to fix it, Vanilla.

00:20:39.700 --> 00:20:41.700
I got the recipe, but it's not mine.

00:20:42.340 --> 00:20:43.850
What do you mean by that?

00:20:43.850 --> 00:20:49.290
No matter what the subject is for the finals, I'm gonna battle with my own original tastes!

00:20:51.370 --> 00:20:53.380
Of course.

00:20:53.380 --> 00:20:56.480
You're gonna work double tomorrow to make up for not practicing today, got it?

00:20:56.910 --> 00:20:57.760
Yup!

00:21:00.620 --> 00:21:01.650
Grandma...

00:21:02.410 --> 00:21:08.520
Your recipe for the strawberry tart made me realise something very important.

00:21:09.300 --> 00:21:13.670
I'm going to do my best in the finals with my precious friends!

00:21:14.640 --> 00:21:16.800
Thank you, grandma.

